think Sized the clone before choosing its shape: 3.2M shallow against our own 451M. Modest, and as a gitlink submodule none of it enters our history at all, which is the convention this room already keeps.
obs License read from its own LICENSE file rather than a summary -- MIT, Copyright uutils developers. Pinned e0ff0ebf29, dated today, so this is the living edge rather than a tag.
obs What it holds itself to is the part worth thanking: matching GNU's output, stdout and error code, exactly, with differences treated as bugs and the count of passing GNU tests published. That is a measurement anyone can re-run rather than an intention anyone can admire, which is the promise this tree makes to itself in a different room.
obs Of the seventeen utilities our guards lean on hardest, it implements all seventeen -- and three of those sit outside POSIX entirely: mktemp, removed from the standard in 2008 and 353 sites here, plus readlink and stat. Those three are where a portable answer is hardest to find because there is no standard to appeal to.
obs The absence is the finding rather than a gap. grep, sed, awk and find are not here, and that boundary is correct: grep and find belong to GNU findutils, sed and awk are their own projects again. Verified against an outside source rather than assumed.
obs So the re-grow is TWO undertakings and the clone is what made the line visible. Counted against our own sites: 5,380 covered by this one repository, 3,129 in the text-processing tools that carry whole languages inside them. Read beside dawk the pair says what neither says alone -- dawk showed the re-grow must keep the C-locale byte view, uutils shows how much of the work is already done by someone willing to be measured.
obs The gratitude page first read C+/79 at 43 percent negative sentences, because I had built it around what uutils does not have. Leading with what is brought it to B+/85 without changing one fact. The Gauge reading caught a framing habit, which is what it is for.
obs Kept dawk's lesson: no foreign pin on the operator card. nib_honesty reads any hash-shaped token there as a claim about this repository, so uutils's pin lives in the gratitude catalogue alone.
obs Pheromone can sign now -- tested its wrapper directly, 119 bytes of signature against its own key. Keaton's two config commands did it. Its remaining block is only that git pull refuses to run over an eleven-file staged index, so the commit comes first and then a rebase rather than a fast-forward, since its rows renumber above %418.
loom uutils license=MIT pin=e0ff0ebf29 utilities=109 our_17_covered=17 sites_covered=5380 sites_uncovered=3129
loom gratitude_page register_first=57 register_after=79 composite_first=79 composite_after=85
file gratitude/uutils-coreutils the submodule, whole and unmodified
file gratitude/uutils-coreutils.md the thanks, and the boundary that splits the re-grow in two
file gratitude/README.md one catalogued entry with source, pin and license
think Petrichor's paste arrived mid-lap and the cause was mine, four hours old. %415's refresh clause reads -nt and nothing else, and signing out does not delete the credential -- it REWRITES it with all seven fields, valid JSON, and empty token strings, expiresAt at the Unix epoch. That file is the newest thing on disk.
obs Measured rather than guessed: host 509 bytes with 108-character tokens and a valid expiry; grain-petrichor 281 bytes with zero-length tokens, twelve minutes newer. The elder clause therefore refused to repair it -- correct by its own rule, wrong by every other measure.
obs The direction of the failure is what makes it worth a row rather than a fix. This is a REPLICATION clause, so a wrong reading does not stay local: petrichor was one launch away from copying emptiness back to the host and onward to every tree. One logged-out checkout would have become three.
obs Freshness is not fitness. A timestamp says nothing about whether contents still work, and the repair reads usability FIRST -- a non-empty accessToken of sixteen characters or more, the cheapest honest test, phoning nowhere. A logged-out host now says so once rather than replicating its emptiness.
obs Proven by doing: petrichor's room went from 281 bytes and dead to 509 and live on the first run of the repaired launcher. And the first attempt failed instructively -- I ran petrichor's OWN launcher, which still holds the elder clause, so the fix only reaches a tree once it lands and pulls.
obs %414's brake did its job here. Petrichor stopped after three fast failures naming it an invocation fault, which is exactly what it was; the loop was right and the launcher was wrong.
loom credential host_bytes=509 petrichor_before=281 petrichor_after=509 tokens_before=0 tokens_after=108 newer_but_dead=yes
file tools/ag/agent-jail.sh usability read before freshness, and a logged-out host announced rather than replicated
file construction/REDS.md %421 -- a newer file is not a better credential
think Keaton asked whether the non-POSIX correction still needed making. Checked xy/main rather than answering from memory: it is published, three matches, amended 20260905.073903. So the answer is done -- but reading the file as a newcomer would showed a fair version of his question I had not asked myself.
obs The correction sat at line 162, after every measurement and after the falsifiers. A reader met 160 lines framed as a bench study before reaching the sentence that reframes all of it. The facts were right and the ORDER taught the wrong thing first.
obs Fixed with a read-this-first block at the head rather than a rewrite, and the block says why the argument still sits where it sits: the measurements came first in time, and this tree keeps the order it learned things in. Accrete rather than restructure -- a dated study that reorders itself to look prescient is a study that has stopped being testimony.
file external-research/yonder/20260905-064341_what-a-harness-promises-about-its-tools.md the head now carries the correction a reader needs before the numbers
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- pheromone's commit and rebase are two commands at the pier shell; toybox is next in the fetch order whenever you want it
